    "notes": "The Communion of the faithful: the showing of the Host, the priest's threefold Dómine non sum dignus, said facing those about to receive, and the form said to each of them. The three repetitions are encoded as three sets of words with their own ids, as at ordinarium.panem-caelestem and in the Kyrie. The one word that separates the two forms is TUAM at w067, where the priest's own form has meam. ECCE at w001 and w004 is tagged intj; Whitaker's heads it so, Collatinus carries it with no features at all, and the corpus's recorded classification ruling lets an analyzer call an interjection an adverb without counting as a divergence. The rubric at s01 prints ad communicandos as one word in witness do; the corpus sets the space, which the 1962 typical edition prints. Witness do alone prints a Confiteor and an absolution before Ecce Agnus Dei; the hand missal begins at Ecce Agnus Dei, and the 1962 rubrics stand with it — n. 503 has Communion within Mass proceed omissis confessione et absolutione, only the Ecce Agnus Dei and the threefold Dómine non sum dignus being said. What do prints there belongs to the recension before 1961: its Confiteor is the corpus's ordinarium.confiteor, and its absolution is the rail's own form — peccatórum vestrórum, vobis, where ordinarium.misereatur has nostrórum, nobis — which the corpus does not carry.",
